('111.7.b.10.E',3,'A family''s income is $2,000 a month and their expenses are $2,200. Which is a way to balance the budget?','["raise expenses by $200", "stop tracking the budget", "lower expenses by $200 or more", "borrow $200 every month"]'::jsonb,2,'Expenses must come down (or income go up) by at least the $200 gap.','original'),
('111.7.b.10.E',3,'Which expense is easiest to cut back when money is short?','["electricity", "groceries", "rent", "eating out"]'::jsonb,3,'Wants like eating out are easier to cut than needs like rent and groceries.','original'),
('111.7.b.10.E',4,'A family has $150 more in expenses than income. Which pair of actions could balance the budget?','["cut $100 from wants and earn $50 more", "do nothing for three months", "cut $50 from wants and add $100 in credit card debt", "add $100 to wants and earn $50 more"]'::jsonb,0,'$100 saved plus $50 earned closes the $150 gap.','original'),
